tools.description:
Accessibility for application windows. Linux and Windows: observe with root rN and read_text reads bounded pages of full name, value, or description; follow next_read. Modes: apps lists confirmed windows (wN, title, app, active) and reports incomplete inventories; missing windows then remain unknown. observe returns the window tree with rN refs. find returns matching rN. act runs ordered steps, checks them before input, stops at the first failed step, and reports each target's change, windows opened/closed/focused, and a diff. activate with wN or title switches the batch target for later refs and ref-less steps. Other-window refs fail until another activate selects their window. Each step reports its window; final observation uses the last executed window. Copy rN/wN exactly; stale refs fail. keypress/type without ref use the batch target, initially the focused window unless refs or window_ref select it. select marks ref, its text substring, or ref..to_ref (paragraphs, cells) and reports the selection read back. activate/close take a title substring or wN. A wait step sends no input and fails the batch on timeout: window (title, any app), query (as find), ref with value/state/text, or text; gone inverts. settle needs no prediction: it waits until the UI changes after the step before it and stops changing; it fails only if nothing changed. After a window wait, keys go to that window, after settle to the focused one. Skip waits the report answers. Errors return code and hint. Examples:
{"mode":"act","actions":[{"type":"click","ref":"r12"},{"type":"wait","window":"Export"}]}
{"mode":"find","window_ref":"w2","query":{"role":"button","name_contains":"Save"}}
